  "scope_limits": [
    "This is a patient-cluster and held-out-split adaptation of the reference-set test, not the complete original image-level5fold/1000subset experiment",
    "The test is cohort-level20-vs20, not inference for a single patient with2 photos",
    "Existing selection40 has been repeatedly inspected; eight p-values are exploratory, correlated, and unadjusted, not confirmatory error-control evidence",
    "Reference patients are nonmembers of the additional NIH target training; original base pretraining membership is unknown",
    "The same-distribution/independent-patient null is an assumption, not proved by equal sample counts or manifest membership",
    "A distribution difference can reflect A/B cohort or E/U image differences; it is not a causal attribution to individual patient training",
    "The released evaluator returns two-sided p although the paper specifies one-sided Welch; retain both without relabelling or selecting the favorable one",
    "Do not equate t-test p or calculated test power with measured patient FPR; no false-positive benchmark is created here",
    "A score is source predict_proba then patient image mean, not logistic decision_function; nonlinear transforms change the t-test",
    "No new comparison method, direction, sample count, p-value threshold, or outcome-dependent stop rule is chosen"
  ],
